& [SelectedFirstSlice]
  + RIS-P0 is one pure platform-neutral runtime-closure manifest compiler and independent verifier
  + it consumes supplied exact machine forms and emits a deterministic zero-effect plan and verification disposition
  + it does not read files inspect a host build acquire write install activate delete clean or contact a provider
  + physical materialization host packaging and runtime activation remain RIS-P1 RIS-P2 and RIS-P3 under separate future source and signatures

& [FormationOrder]
  + bind the exact two-root seed meaning and bootstrap descriptor without claiming that SOP contains third-party bytes
  + define strict material prerequisite source target edge closure plan verification receipt unresolved denial and nonauthority forms
  + choose conservative platform-neutral logical path and content-identity rules for P0
  + define finite graph parser text byte and evidence ceilings
  + derive closure reachability producer uniqueness acyclicity topological ordering target collision and ambient-input refusal
  + reconcile existing seeded-compiler Slice5 candidate Slice6 receipt PreparedRuntime and SOP boot-session boundaries by exact identity only
  + perform dual-hemisphere threat pruning seven-fold and feature-requirement support reviews
  + emit canonical specification explosion justification solution implementation plan matrix phase lock proof review formation verifier and satisfaction signature
  + publish formation remote equal and replay it before considering Rust

& [ConservativeP0Decisions]
  + first fixture is platform-neutral and fully synthetic with no operating-system file contact
  + every material node has exact lower-case SHA256 expected bytes and one closed material kind
  + roots are exactly one admitted bootstrap-runtime descriptor and one admitted installation-SOP descriptor
  + logical target paths use slash-separated relative UTF-8 segments with no empty dot dot-dot drive UNC device link case-collision or alternate-stream semantics
  + graph order is derived rather than trusted and equal semantic inputs yield byte-identical canonical output
  + source build acquired and explicitly supplied nodes describe expected results but do not perform their transforms
  + secrets are opaque external-custody references and are never material bytes in P0
  + host operating-system driver firmware hardware network and artifact availability remain declared prerequisites not inferred closure members

& [ProposedAcceptance]
  + a complete small synthetic runtime closure compiles validates serializes and byte-identically replays twice
  + every node is reachable from the two roots through exact producer edges and every runtime target has one unambiguous producer
  + unknown duplicate overbound cyclic unreachable missing-source hash byte path target producer order authority and effect mutations refuse without partial output
  + an independent verifier reconstructs the entire output from retained supplied inputs and rejects raw-byte or semantic tampering
  + focused debug overflow-checked release warnings-denied lint format exact workspace evidence attribution publication and post-push replay gates pass

& [StopRules]
  + stop before canonical signature if any material kind transform path rule closure invariant bound or acceptance fixture remains ambiguous
  + stop before Rust unless the satisfaction signature binds exact requirements and zero-effect authority
  + stop on hidden ambient dependency mutable unpinned identity self-signature installation laundering secret embedding or activation implication

& [StillGated]
  + actual bootstrap binary selection compiler download dependency vendoring artifact pack creation model acquisition license acceptance filesystem access build process network install permission service activation cleanup rollback remote machine FPGA Minecraft and every physical effect
